          "summary": "The U.S. Senate rejected cloture on H.R. 3633, the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act, by 49 votes to 50, well below the 60 votes required to advance. No Democrats supported the motion; Republican senators Susan Collins, Josh Hawley, Jerry Moran and Thom Tillis voted no, while Chris Coons did not vote. Tillis changed his vote to preserve the option of reconsideration. With Congress preparing to leave Washington ahead of the November midterms, the bill is effectively on hold and durable federal rules dividing SEC and CFTC authority remain unresolved, although executive agencies may continue rulemaking.",
